// @x in an assertion is the final value at location x, not the location.
//
// MoRDor's own test. The pair with atloc-unwritten.lit is the point: one file
// asserts the value that is written and the other forbids one that is not, so
// a regression that makes @x a free variable again fails the second even though
// the first still passes.
//
// It did make it a free variable: the lexer bound '@x' including the '@', while
// the memory state Assertion.ConditionChecker builds is keyed by the bare
// location name, so the substitution silently missed and every @ assertion was
// decided against an unconstrained symbol (#84). allow (@x = 999999) was true
// on a program that never writes it.
x := 0;
x := 7;
%% allow (@x = 7) []
